{"ver": "0.1", "info": {"id": "XsX3Dl", "date": "1399349087", "viewed": 250, "name": "Dyadic transformation", "username": "Mx7f", "description": "An implmentation of Dyadic transformation, also known as the Bit shift map. http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bit_shift_map", "likes": 3, "published": 1, "flags": 0, "usePreview": 0, "tags": ["2d", "dyadic"], "hasliked": 0, "parentid": "", "parentname": ""}, "renderpass": [{"inputs": [], "outputs": [], "code": "float dyadicIteration(float x) {\n\treturn x < 0.5 ? 2.*x : 2.*x-1.;\t\n}\n\n#define ITERATIONS 20\n\nvoid mainImage( out vec4 fragColor, in vec2 fragCoord )\n{\n\tvec2 v = (fragCoord.xy-0.5*iResolution.xy) / iResolution.x;\n\tfloat x = length(v);\n\tfloat alpha = sin(iTime)*0.40+0.5;\n\tfloat c = 0.0;\n\tfor(int i = 0; i < ITERATIONS; ++i) {\n\t\tx = dyadicIteration(x);\n\t\tc = alpha*c+(1.0-alpha)*x;\n\t}\n\t\n\tfragColor = vec4(vec3(c),1.0);\n}", "name": "", "description": "", "type": "image"}]}